  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The evidence submitted fails to demonstrate that the single\r\nstorey rear extension at&amp;nbsp;66 Whitmore Road, West Harrow, Harrow, HA1\r\n4AD&amp;nbsp;was&amp;nbsp;in situ and in use as part of the main dwellinghouse for a\r\ncontinuous period of at least 4 years prior to the date of this application on\r\n3rd December 2025.&amp;nbsp;The construction of the single storey rear extension is\r\ntherefore not immune from enforcement action under S.171B of the Town and\r\nCountry Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and is lawful under Section 191 of the\r\nTown and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;height: 93.7pt;&quot;&gt;The proposal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Certificate of Lawful Existing Development: Single storey side to rear extension; External alterations (Demolition of attached garage) fails to fall within the parameters&lt;span style=&quot;height:93.7pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of permitted development as set out under Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A.1(j)(iii),&amp;nbsp;Class A.1(ja) and Class A.3(a)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;height: 93.7pt;&quot;&gt;of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
